Create a 100x100 two-dimensional byte array to represent the maze.
Each byte in the array will represent a cell in the maze.
Each byte in this array will have a value of 0, 1, 2, or 3.
A value of 0 means the cell has no walls.
A value of 1 means the cell has a top wall.
A value of 2 means the cell has a left wall.
A value of 3 means the cell has both a top and a left wall.
Randomly assign the contents of the maze as follows
* 10% of the cells will have the value 1
* 10% of the cells will have the value 2
* 10% of the cells will have the value 3
All other cells will have the value 0.

Each cell in the maze will be 32x32 pixels in size.
Create three sprite shapes to correspond to the 1,2,3 values in the map array.
The first should have the top row of pixels set to blue
The second should have the leftmost column of pixels set to blue
The third should have both the top row and leftmost column of pixels set to blue.

Use these sprites to draw the map on the screen.
The user should see the exact middle of the map, pixel-wise
Display 8 columns and 7 rows of the maze

In the game's main loop, poll the joystick and move the viewport up, down, left, or right accordingly

